{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Aharon shall come into the Tent of Meeting.</b> Our Rabbis said that this is not the place of this verse, and they gave the reason for their words in tractate Yoma (32a). And they said: the entire passage is stated in order, except for this entry, which is after the offering of his burnt-offering and the burnt-offering of the people, and the burning of the emurs of the bull and the goat, which are performed outside in the golden garments; and he immerses and sanctifies and strips them off and dons the white garments — <b>and he comes into the Tent of Meeting</b> to take out the ladle and the firepan with which he burned the incense in the innermost sanctum." "<b>And he shall strip off the linen garments.</b> After he has taken it out. And he dons the golden garments for the afternoon tamid. And this is the order of the services: the morning tamid in golden garments; the service of the inner bull and goat and the incense of the firepan in white garments; the ram and the ram of the people and some of the additional offerings in golden garments; the taking out of the ladle and firepan in white garments; the rest of the additional offerings and the afternoon tamid and the incense of the Hekhal upon the inner altar in golden garments. And the order of the verses according to the services is thus: ״וְשִׁלַּח אֶת הַשָּׂעִיר בַּמִּדְבָּר״, ״וְרָחַץ אֶת בְּשָׂרוֹ בַמַּיִם״ and so on, ״וְיָצָא וְעָשָׂה אֶת עֹלָתוֹ״ and so on, ״וְאֵת חֵלֶב הַחַטָּאת״ and so on, and the entire passage until ״וְאַחֲרֵי כֵן יָבֹא אֶל הַמַּחֲנֶה״ — and afterward, ״וּבָא אַהֲרֹן״." "<b>And he shall leave them there.</b> This teaches that they require גניזה (storage/retiring), and he may not use those four garments on another Yom HaKippurim (Yoma 12a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:53.305122766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}